# Cursor Main Rules

Rule Type: Always

## Core Development Principles
- Follow SOLID, DRY, KISS principles consistently
- Prefer minimal code changes to achieve tasks
- Write testable, mockable code
- Use early returns for error conditions
- Implement proper error handling at function start

## Code Quality Standards
- Validate all inputs thoroughly
- Use meaningful, descriptive names
- Keep functions focused and small
- Avoid code duplication
- Comment complex logic explaining "why", not "what"

## Project Structure Awareness
- Use .instructions/ for task-specific guidance
- Follow validation gates (Level 0-3) after changes
- Always run format-code.ps1 before commits
- Use scratchpad/ for complex work documentation
- Reference shared types from shared/types/

## Technology Stack
- Frontend: SvelteKit 5.0 + TypeScript + Tailwind
- Backend: ASP.NET 9.0 + Orleans + SignalR + EF Core
- Database: SQLite with EF Core
- AI: LmDotnetTools suite

## Key Patterns
- Messages flow through MessageRouter.svelte
- Real-time updates via SignalR
- Orleans grains for state management
- Structured logging for debugging
- Dual mode operation (Orleans/Direct)

